<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kidal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kidal is a town in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adrar-des-ifoghas">Adrar des Ifoghas</a> mountains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. It is the main centre of the Kel Adagh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> and was founded as a French post in the early 20th century. Since independence it has been at the heart of repeated Tuareg rebellions against the Malian state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kidal.jpg" alt="Kidal" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Taguelmoust at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maison_artisans.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
